  "body": "Records the post-#8316 many_worlds re-measurement for #7064 (queue task 12126), the resume step the task was dep-blocked on until the bench could run clean again.\n\n**The run** — full `cargo bench --offline --bench world_bench` at `main` a824f622ae on the reference machine (AMD Ryzen 7 7840U, 16 threads, Linux 6.18.60, NixOS; rustc 1.99.0; laptop under shared fleet load), exit 0:\n\n```text\nbench many_worlds unit=ms_per_command median=1065.462 min=4.841 reps=1 p50_ms=1065.462 p95_ms=3602.663 p99_ms=4549.272 target_p99_ms=50 target_met=false idle_worlds=1000 active_worlds=100 events_per_second=20 duration_secs=10 commands=20000 load_elapsed_secs=12.784 completed_events_per_second=1564.5 checkpoint_triggers=100 checkpoints=100 evicted=100 reopened=100\n```\n\n- Clean run: the restore path that failed pre-#8316 now passes; checkpoint/evict/reopen assertions hold for all 100 active worlds (100/100/100).\n- p99 4,549.272 ms vs the 2026-11-02 reference 5,650.792 ms — **−1,101.520 ms (−19.5%)**; completed throughput 1,564.5/s vs 1,523.1/s. Target still **not** met (50 ms), as expected before the fix lands.\n- `journal_append_fsync` this run: median 5,443.164 µs — in line with the 5,180 µs reference, confirming the #7064 profiling verdict stands: per-append fdatasync queueing dominates p99.\n\n**Changes** (records only, no code):\n\n- `pkgs/id/benches/baseline.txt` — the new many_worlds line appended under a dated comment; all existing lines unchanged.\n- `pkgs/id/benches/BASELINES.md` — a dated re-measurement block after the 2026-11-02 reference, with the delta, the integrity result, and the remaining-gap statement.\n\n**Remaining gap:** the scoped fix for the dominant phase is the group-commit work split to #8239 (journal `append_batch` + actor-side drain, already queued). #557 stays open until a recorded run shows `target_met=true`; this PR does not close #7064 either — it completes the measurement step task 12126 was blocked on.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797255086&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=10002&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F10002&signature=54e43ce30769bc27c6cd25df4df52ec3b951648141fc2e574b9e30edf0aca6b5\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/10002?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added updated `many_worlds` benchmark results, with improved p99 latency and slightly higher throughput.\n  * Recorded that checkpoint and reopen assertions pass, while the 50 ms p99 target remains unmet. The notes identify per-append sync queueing as the remaining latency gap.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
